.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle build"
creates two kinds of output.
An image is made from a source file and requires only the Wattle
runtime.
Executables,
libraries and WebAssembly programs are made from the exes and
libs that a Wattle project declares in its info file.
A native executable,
a native library and a web program require the Zig toolchain.
.Pp
.Nm "wattle build"
can be invoked using
.Cm wattle b .
.
.Ss Subcommands
An image is made from a source file,
not from a project’s info file,
and requires nothing further.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Cm img
.Xc
Loads the module at
.Ar source
and writes an image of its environment to
.Ar output .
If
.Ar output
is omitted,
it is
.Ar source
with
.Ql "\&.wattle"
replaced by
.Ql "\&.wimage" .
.Xr wattle-run 1
can be used to load the image later.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-lib"
.Ar module
.Xc
Imports
.Ar module
into the environment before
.Ar source
is loaded,
as
.Ic "wattle run"
does.
Several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.El
.El
.Pp
Executables,
libraries and web programs are made from the declarations in
the project’s info file.
The generated files are in
.Ql "zig-out"
in the project root,
and a copied or fetched library is in
.Ql "\&.wattle" .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
