.Ss Zig toolchain
Building executables,
native libraries and web programs requires:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Cm zig
to be on the user’s
.Ev PATH .
.It
The Wattle source,
which is included in Wattle releases and which is installed
to
.Ql "<prefix>/share/wattle" .
.El
.Pp
No Zig build files are required.
.Nm "wattle build"
creates temporary
.Ql "build\&.zig"
and
.Ql "build\&.zig\&.zon"
files from the declarations in the project’s info file.
It then uses these to build with
.Cm zig .
Copying a source library needs no Zig,
and fetching a remote library needs
.Cm git
or
.Cm curl
and
.Cm tar .
.Pp
The project’s info file is
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory.
.
.Ss Declarations
A project author declares what the project builds in three vectors
of the project’s info file:
.Ql ":exes" ,
.Ql ":libs"
and
.Ql ":docs" .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :exes \(lB{:type :native
         :name \(dqhello\(dq
         :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq}\(rB
 :libs \(lB{:type :native
         :name \(dqgreet\(dq
         :root \(dqgreet\&.zig\(dq
         :for \(lB\(dqhello\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.Pp
Every exe and lib has a
.Ql ":type"
and a
.Ql ":name" ,
a string of letters,
digits,
.Ql "_"
and
.Ql "-" .
A name is unique among the exes,
and among the libs.
A doc has a
.Ql ":type"
and no
.Ql ":name" .
.Pp
An exe has an
.Ql ":entry" ,
the file where
.Ql "main"
is defined,
and one of these types:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":native"
.Xc
A standalone executable that
.Cm exe
builds.
.It Xo
.Ql ":source"
.Xc
A program that
.Ql "wattle apps install"
installs as source.
.Nm "wattle build"
does not build it.
It also requires
.Ql ":files" ,
a vector of the paths to install.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.It Xo
.Ql ":web"
.Xc
A program for a browser that
.Cm web
builds.
.El
.Pp
A lib may have
.Ql ":for" ,
a vector of the names of the exes it is part of.
A native exe is built with each native lib whose
.Ql ":for"
names it,
and a web exe takes no lib.
A lib has one of these types:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":native"
.Xc
A native module.
It requires
.Ql ":root" ,
the Zig root file.
.It Xo
.Ql ":source"
.Xc
Wattle source.
It requires
.Ql ":files" ,
a vector of paths.
Each is copied to the same path under
.Ql "\&.wattle/<name>/" ,
so
.Ql ":files \(lB\(dqutil/\(dq\(rB"
puts
.Ql "util/init\&.wattle"
at
.Ql "\&.wattle/util/util/init\&.wattle" ,
which is imported as
.Ql "\*(lpimport util/util\*(rp" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":remote"
.Xc
A lib that is fetched from
.Ql ":url" ,
a Git repository or a URL ending in
.Ql "\&.tar"
or
.Ql "\&.tar\&.gz" .
A Git repository requires
.Ql ":ref" ,
a branch or tag,
and a tarball requires
.Ql ":hash" ,
.Ql "sha256:"
and the tree hash of its files as
.Ql "wattle apps install"
records it under
.Ql ":rev" .
The source must have an info file that declares a lib of the
same
.Ql ":name" ,
as
.Ql ":native"
or
.Ql ":source" ,
and the lib takes that form.
A lib is fetched again only when its
.Ql ":url" ,
.Ql ":ref"
or
.Ql ":hash"
changes.
.El
.Pp
A doc requires
.Ql ":files"
and may have
.Ql ":for" .
A
.Ql ":man"
doc is a set of manual pages,
each named with a period and its section,
as in
.Ql "hello\&.1" .
A
.Ql ":web"
doc is a set of files for a web exe.
.Pp
The info file may not have
.Ql ":artifacts"
or
.Ql ":man" ,
and an exe may not have
.Ql ":libs" .
.Nm "wattle build"
names what replaces each.
.
.Ss Web programs
Web programs are exes that are designed to run in a browser environment.
To do this,
.Nm "wattle build"
.Cm web
creates four files in
.Ql "zig-out/web/<name>/" :
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "wattle-<hash>\&.wasm" ,
the runtime
.It
.Ql "<name>-<hash>\&.wimage" ,
the program
.It
.Ql "wasi-<hash>\&.js" ,
the WASI support shim
.It
.Ql "<name>\&.js" ,
an ES module that exports
.Ql "load"
and
.Ql "run"
.El
.Pp
Example programs are distributed with the Wattle source tree.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compile a program into an image and run the image:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle build img hello\&.wattle hello\&.wimage
$ wattle run -i hello\&.wimage Alice
.Ed
.Pp
Build the native executables that the project’s info file declares,
optimised for size:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle -p /usr/local build exe --release small
.Ed
.
